{
  "info": {
    "name": "Miqaat Identity Federation",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "## Run order\n1. **1. Sign in**, top to bottom. `Portal page` saves `transaction_id` + `csrf`; `POST /login` saves the CORE `role_id`; the two `select-scope` requests save `access_token` (Authorization API) and `admin_identity_access_token` (Identity admin). Both are also stored as globals `access_token` / `identity_access_token`, which the *Miqaat Core Identity Authorization* collection uses.\n2. **2. Client administration** after changing a client in the Authorization collection.\n3. **3. Embedded login**: `Create transaction` → `Embedded login page` → `Authenticate`.\n\n## CSRF\nBrowser endpoints (`/login`, `/select-scope`, `/portal/*`, `/embed/*`) need `Origin: {{identity}}` (exactly: `localhost`, not `127.0.0.1`) and `X-CSRF-Token` from the page boot JSON, with the matching `transaction_id`. These requests send both. The pair is valid for 5 minutes before sign-in; after a portal sign-in it is bound to that session for the session lifetime. On `403 CSRF_VALIDATION_FAILED`, `details.reason` says why: re-run `Portal page` (or `Embedded login page`).\n\n## Cookies and secrets\nPostman's cookie jar keeps `federation_session` for localhost. `401 SESSION_REQUIRED` means it is missing: run `POST /login` again or check Cookies → localhost. Put `password` in the *current value* only so it is never exported."
  },
